 "title": "6-pin DIP high dv/dt random-phase triac drivers: FOD420, FOD4208, FOD4216, FOD4218",
 "source": {
  "document": "FOD4218/D",
  "revision": "Rev. 5, February 2026",
  "pages": 13
 },
 "summary": "An optocoupler whose infrared LED fires a hybrid random-phase triac, built from two SCRs in inverse parallel, for triggering a discrete power triac or SCR pair; it is not meant to drive a load by itself. FOD420 and FOD4216 block 600 V, FOD4208 and FOD4218 block 800 V. FOD4216 and FOD4218 use a higher-efficiency LED and trigger at 1.3 mA maximum against 2 mA for the other two. Static dv/dt is 10,000 V/µs minimum and isolation 5,000 VACRMS for one minute, in through-hole DIP or surface-mount lead-bend 6-pin packages.",
