 "circuits": [
  {
   "id": "hot-line",
   "title": "Hot-line switching application circuit",
   "page": 5,
   "description": "The driver fires a power triac (FKPF12N80) that switches the hot side of a 240 VAC line, with the load between the triac and neutral; the load may equally sit on the hot side. A NAND gate output sinks the LED current through Rin from VCC. Rin is sized so IF equals the chosen part's rated IFT: 2 mA for FOD420 and FOD4208, 1.3 mA for FOD4216 and FOD4218. When the LED is lit the driver's output connects the hot line through 360 Ω to the triac gate; 330 Ω runs from gate to MT1. The 39 Ω and 0.01 µF series pair across the triac is a snubber whose need depends on the triac and the load.",
