 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Structure",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "An infrared LED is optically coupled to a random-phase triac made of two SCRs in inverse parallel. FOD4216 and FOD4218 carry a high-efficiency LED that gives them a lower trigger current."
  },
  {
   "topic": "LED drive",
   "page": 4,
   "text": "Every unit is guaranteed to fire at or below its maximum IFT, so IF is set between that value (1.3 mA for FOD4216 and FOD4218, 2 mA for FOD420 and FOD4208) and the 30 mA continuous rating. In the application circuits the input resistor Rin is chosen so that IF equals the rated IFT."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Use as a driver only",
   "page": 5,
   "text": "The part triggers an external triac or a pair of SCRs; it is not to switch a load directly."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Snubber",
   "page": 5,
   "text": "The 39 Ω and 0.01 µF network across the power triac in the hot-line circuit may not be needed; that depends on the triac and the load. With highly inductive loads (power factor below 0.5) the 39 Ω becomes 360 Ω."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Load position",
   "page": 5,
   "text": "In hot-line switching the triac sits in the hot line and the load connects to neutral, though the load may be put on either the neutral or the hot side."
  },
  {
   "topic": "dv/dt ratings",
   "page": 4,
   "text": "The 10,000 V/µs figure is static dv/dt across the output. Commutating dv/dt is set by the thyristors the part drives, not by the part."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Isolation test",
   "page": 4,
   "text": "VISO is tested with the input pins 1, 2, 3 shorted together and the output pins 4, 5, 6 shorted together. A 1 minute test at 5,000 VACRMS counts the same as 1 second at 6,000 VACRMS."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Safety approvals",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "UL1577 recognised at 5,000 VACRMS for 1 minute. DIN EN/IEC 60747-5-5 approval applies to the parts ordered with the V option; such parts carry a V in their marking. Pb-free and RoHS compliant."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Marking",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "The top carries the onsemi logo, the device number (for example FOD420), a V for the DIN EN/IEC 60747-5-5 option when ordered, a one-digit year code (X), a two-digit work week (YY) and an assembly package code (D)."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Soldering",
   "page": 8,
   "text": "Reflow: ramp at 2 to 10 °C/s, keep the time above 183 °C at 160 s or less, spend 10 to 30 s near 245 °C with a profile peak of 260 °C; the package surface peak is 262 °C. Reflow once only. Lead solder temperature is rated 260 °C for 10 s."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Ordering",
   "page": 8,
   "text": "Suffixes apply to all four families: none for the through-hole DIP, S for the surface-mount lead-bend form in tubes, SD for it on tape and reel (1000), V adds the DIN EN/IEC 60747-5-5 option, and TV is the DIP with 0.4 inch lead spacing and the V option. Tubes hold 50."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Applications",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Named uses: solid-state relays, static power switches, AC motor starters, and lighting and industrial controls."
  }
